cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: physio-import
abstract: Reads cardiovascular and autonomic physiology recordings from common acquisition systems (EDF/EDF+/BDF,
  WFDB, Axon ABF, Spike2 .smr, BIOPAC .acq, NWB, HDF5, MATLAB .mat including LabChart and Spike2 exports,
  CSV/TSV/XLSX and LabChart text exports, WAV) and writes one NWB file per recording with typed and, where the
  source gives a unit, calibrated channels (ECG, blood pressure, respiration, PPG, nerve, EMG, stimulation,
  heart rate, temperature, other pressures), the source's markers and per-trial stimulation parameters, plus
  recordings.csv, channels.csv and events.tsv index tables. Every NWB file is checked with NWB Inspector; each
  channel is checked for flat, saturated and noisy stretches and shown in an overview figure. The first step of
  the Cardiovascular Response to Nerve Stimulation and Heart Rate Variability and Baroreflex workflows. Built on
  Neo, WFDB for Python, pyEDFlib, PyNWB and bioread.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/physio-import
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- physiology
- autonomic
- cardiovascular
- ecg
- blood-pressure
- respiration
- nerve-stimulation
- electrophysiology
- nwb
- data-import
- quality-control
